    {
      "name": "The Nodrum",
      "type": "text",
      "_id": "DYwOepNDMTv9ds8W",
      "title": {
        "show": true,
        "level": 1
      },
      "image": {},
      "text": {
        "format": 1,
        "content": "<p><strong>Type:</strong> Landmark<br><strong>First Visited:</strong> @UUID[Compendium.grimwild-kb.kb.JournalEntry.jir5X1jFd08ME0H1]{Session 2}</p>\n<h2>Description</h2>\n<p>An ancient stone facility built into the side of a mountain at the nexus of several ley lines, deep in @UUID[Compendium.grimwild-kb.kb.JournalEntry.aHJXqousaIFYnECh]{Marrow County}, not far from @UUID[Compendium.grimwild-kb.kb.JournalEntry.E6jtdcGA7bfRGvuj]{Aurelion}.<br>Once known as the Nexarium (or Aurelion Vault), it was originally a magical prison constructed during the wars of the @UUID[Compendium.grimwild-kb.kb.JournalEntry.jB7eRLPu6CNxnyYm]{Old Gods} to contain @UUID[Compendium.grimwild-kb.kb.JournalEntry.03mz8edEPYw7i0UL]{The Xan-Kor}, a construct of the God of Forgetting.<br>The facade bears geometric glyphs of immense age, overlaid with Luciferian architectural stonework that has since worn away.</p>\n<h2>Notable Features</h2>\n<ul><li>@UUID[Compendium.grimwild-kb.kb.JournalEntry.Pom8bgcTgRw75seF]{The Triune} have retrofitted it with halfling-sized structures and equipment, including rotating platforms, mirrors, and lenses for their geometric magic</li><li>Clockwork constructs serve as workers and guardians; clockwork spiders maintain the machinery</li><li>Contains an antechamber library with history books documenting its origins as the Nexarium</li><li>A central chamber with a deep pit where @UUID[Compendium.grimwild-kb.kb.JournalEntry.03mz8edEPYw7i0UL]{The Xan-Kor} is held</li><li>The door has been rebuilt at a middle size — large for halflings but tight for humans</li><li>Sits at the nexus of several ley lines, making it a site of immense magical power</li></ul>\n<h2>Connected Locations</h2>\n<ul><li>@UUID[Compendium.grimwild-kb.kb.JournalEntry.E6jtdcGA7bfRGvuj]{Aurelion} - Nearby capital city of @UUID[Compendium.grimwild-kb.kb.JournalEntry.aHJXqousaIFYnECh]{Marrow County}</li><li>@UUID[Compendium.grimwild-kb.kb.JournalEntry.aHJXqousaIFYnECh]{Marrow County} - The county in which the Nodrum is located</li></ul>\n<h2>Associated NPCs</h2>\n<ul><li>@UUID[Compendium.grimwild-kb.kb.JournalEntry.Pom8bgcTgRw75seF]{The Triune} - Current occupants who unlocked and retrofitted the abandoned facility</li></ul>\n<h2>Events Here</h2>\n<ul><li>@UUID[Compendium.grimwild-kb.kb.JournalEntry.jir5X1jFd08ME0H1]{Session 2} - The party sought the Triune&#x27;s help with the ruin crisis; the Triune examined @UUID[Compendium.grimwild-kb.kb.JournalEntry.6Eqkl1MNE1055IJC]{Edric}, revealed the old gods&#x27; history of ruin and renewal, and confessed to siphoning @UUID[Compendium.grimwild-kb.kb.JournalEntry.crg1JpVHgdUHPdOO]{Castor}&#x27;s curse energy; a ritual to contain the Xan-Kor succeeded but corrupted ley lines and reality itself; the Triune declared the party were the heralds of ruin</li></ul>",
        "markdown": ""
      },
